{"max_tokens":8192,"messages":[{"content":[{"cache_control":{"type":"ephemeral"},"text":"Research brief: The height of Olympus Mons in miles, and a listed price in 2019.\n\nSubquestion sq-2: what was the listed price in 2019\nTime frame: 2019-01-01 to 2019-12-31\nToday's date: 2026-11-25","type":"text"}],"role":"user"}],"model":"fake-model","system":[{"cache_control":{"type":"ephemeral"},"text":"You are a research subagent inside a verification harness, assigned ONE subquestion. Gather evidence for it and record premises. You will not write any answer — a separate writer will, using only recorded premises and findings. Anything you do not record is lost.\n\nWorkflow:\n1. search_broad to find relevant pages.\n2. fetch promising URLs. fetch returns span IDs (doc:<hash>#<start>-<end>) with text previews.\n3. record_premises for every fact you may need: atomic statements (one subject, one predicate, under 300 characters), quantities exactly as the span states them, span_refs listing the supporting span IDs. Set claim_class by mutability: \"stable\" for facts that do not change, \"slow\" for slowly-changing facts (populations, rankings), \"volatile\" for prices, versions, and roles. Rejected premises come back with reasons — fix and re-record. Record premises as soon as you have their spans — you have a hard turn cap, and anything unrecorded when it hits is lost. Do not save recording for one final batch.\n4. When done, call submit_report exactly once: status (answered / partial / blocked), findings derived from your recorded premises (each cites premise IDs), conflicts between premises, and dead_ends (queries that yielded nothing, so they are not re-issued).\n\nRules:\n- Numbers and quoted phrases in a premise must appear exactly in a cited span. A premise states only what its source states.\n- A figure you derive — a unit conversion, sum, difference, ratio, percent change or rounding — is never a premise. Submit it in submit_report as a finding with edge_type \"computes\" and an operation: the operands are numbers taken from premises you recorded (premise id plus the value as that premise states it), and the harness recomputes the output. If the arithmetic is wrong the finding comes back with the correct value.\n- Every number in any other finding must appear in the premises that finding cites.\n- A premise must stand alone: name the specific entity (never a bare \"it\", \"they\", or \"the study\"), state one statement per premise, and give specifics instead of vague terms like \"benefits\" or \"significant\" — vague or ambiguous premises are rejected.\n- Temporal ordering findings (\"X before/after Y\") must cite exactly two premises, in the order the events are mentioned, and the dates must appear in the premises or their spans.\n- Record premises for conflicting evidence too; report conflicts upward, never resolve them silently.\n- If you cannot find usable sources, submit_report with status \"blocked\" and your dead_ends. Do not fabricate.\n- Work only on your assigned subquestion.\n- Your subquestion states the time frame it asks about. When a span says WHEN a fact held, set as_of on that premise to the date as the span gives it (a year, a month and year, a quarter or a full date); the harness checks it appears in the span. Leave as_of out when the span gives no date — never guess one.","type":"text"}],"tools":[{"description":"Fetch a URL and index its content into citable spans. Returns span IDs of the form doc:<hash>#<start>-<end> with short previews. Cite these span IDs in your answer.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"url":{"description":"URL to fetch","minLength":1,"pattern":"^https?://","title":"Url","type":"string"}},"required":["url"],"type":"object"},"name":"fetch"},{"description":"Record atomic factual premises extracted from fetched spans. Each premise: one subject, one predicate, quantities stated exactly as the span states them — a premise never holds a figure you derived: conversions, sums, ratios and the like go in submit_report as computes findings. A premise must stand alone: name the specific entity (never a bare 'it' or 'the study'), and state specifics instead of vague terms like 'benefits' or 'significant'. Keep each premise text under 300 characters — longer ones are rejected; split them. span_refs must be span IDs returned by fetch. Returns premise IDs — your final answer will cite these, so record every fact you intend to use, as soon as you have its spans. Rejected premises include the reason; fix and re-record them. A near-duplicate of an already-recorded premise is not re-recorded: you get the existing premise ID (with any new spans attached as corroboration) — cite that ID instead of rephrasing a known fact. If the span states WHEN the fact held, give that date as as_of — it decides how the fact is weighed against the time the question asks about.","input_schema":{"$defs":{"LenientPremiseDraftV3":{"additionalProperties":false,"description":"One atomic premise, stated exactly as its spans state it.","properties":{"as_of":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"When the fact held, IF the cited span states that date: a year ('2019'), a month and year ('March 2025'), a quarter ('Q3 2025') or a full date ('2025-03-01'). The harness checks the date appears in the span. Omit it when the span gives no date.","title":"As Of"},"claim_class":{"default":"stable","enum":["stable","slow","volatile"],"title":"Claim Class","type":"string"},"span_refs":{"items":{"type":"string"},"minItems":1,"title":"Span Refs","type":"array"},"text":{"minLength":1,"title":"Text","type":"string"}},"required":["text","span_refs"],"title":"LenientPremiseDraftV3","type":"object"}},"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"premises":{"items":{"$ref":"#/$defs/LenientPremiseDraftV3"},"maxItems":20,"minItems":1,"title":"Premises","type":"array"}},"required":["premises"],"type":"object"},"name":"record_premises"},{"description":"Search the web for pages relevant to a query. Returns ranked results with URLs. Use fetch on promising URLs to read them and obtain citable spans.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"k":{"default":5,"description":"Number of results","maximum":10,"minimum":1,"title":"K","type":"integer"},"query":{"description":"Web search query","minLength":1,"title":"Query","type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"type":"object"},"name":"search_broad"},{"description":"Search the text of documents ALREADY fetched in this session for relevant spans. Returns citable span IDs with previews. Use this to re-check gathered evidence before searching the web again.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"k":{"default":5,"description":"Number of spans to return","maximum":10,"minimum":1,"title":"K","type":"integer"},"query":{"description":"What to look for in already-fetched documents","minLength":1,"title":"Query","type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"type":"object"},"name":"search_within"},{"cache_control":{"type":"ephemeral"},"description":"Submit your final report for the assigned subquestion. Call exactly once, after recording all premises. findings must cite premise IDs you recorded.","input_schema":{"$defs":{"Conflict":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"a":{"title":"A","type":"string"},"b":{"title":"B","type":"string"},"note":{"default":"","title":"Note","type":"string"}},"required":["a","b"],"title":"Conflict","type":"object"},"FindingDraftV2":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"edge_type":{"enum":["deduces","induces","temporal","computes"],"title":"Edge Type","type":"string"},"operation":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/$defs/Operation"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"Required when edge_type is 'computes'; omit otherwise"},"premise_ids":{"items":{"type":"string"},"minItems":1,"title":"Premise Ids","type":"array"},"text":{"minLength":1,"title":"Text","type":"string"}},"required":["text","premise_ids","edge_type"],"title":"FindingDraftV2","type":"object"},"Operand":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"premise_id":{"description":"A premise you recorded that states this number","title":"Premise Id","type":"string"},"value":{"description":"The number exactly as that premise states it, e.g. '21.9'","title":"Value","type":"string"}},"required":["premise_id","value"],"title":"Operand","type":"object"},"Operation":{"additionalProperties":false,"description":"A derivation the harness recomputes with exact decimal arithmetic.","properties":{"description":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"op 'other' only: what was done","title":"Description"},"op":{"description":"convert: one operand between unit_from and unit_to. sum: two or more operands. diff: first minus second. ratio: first divided by second. percent_change: from the first operand to the second. round: one operand to `precision`. other: anything else, described in `description` — recorded as UNVERIFIED and never treated as evidence, so prefer a recomputable op.","enum":["convert","sum","diff","ratio","percent_change","round","other"],"title":"Op","type":"string"},"operands":{"items":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Operand"},"minItems":1,"title":"Operands","type":"array"},"output":{"description":"The result as your finding states it, e.g. '13.6'","title":"Output","type":"string"},"precision":{"default":"1","description":"A power of ten the output is rounded to: '1', '0.1', '0.01'","title":"Precision","type":"string"},"unit_from":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"convert only, e.g. 'km'","title":"Unit From"},"unit_to":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"description":"convert only, e.g. 'mi'","title":"Unit To"}},"required":["op","operands","output"],"title":"Operation","type":"object"}},"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Your final report for the assigned subquestion.","properties":{"conflicts":{"items":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Conflict"},"title":"Conflicts","type":"array"},"dead_ends":{"items":{"type":"string"},"title":"Dead Ends","type":"array"},"findings":{"items":{"$ref":"#/$defs/FindingDraftV2"},"title":"Findings","type":"array"},"status":{"enum":["answered","partial","blocked"],"title":"Status","type":"string"},"summary":{"default":"","maxLength":500,"title":"Summary","type":"string"}},"required":["status"],"type":"object"},"name":"submit_report"}]}